<%doc>

=head1 NAME

/breeders_toolbox/weather.mas - Weather page (/breeders/weather)

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Weather for breeding. Research stations (Breedbase locations) on the left;
for the chosen one: 1 the distance range (km or miles, default from the configuration),
2 the weather station (real observing stations within the range: airports,
national weather service (SYNOP) stations, CoCoRaHS, IDEAM, INMET, ANA and
CEMADEN rain gauges, and the stations of research farms whose data users
upload as CSV / Excel: /breeders_toolbox/weather/upload_dialog.mas; a rain
gauge is paired with a station for temperature),
3 the season (dates, crop, planting date or the season of a trial). Tabs:
Season (stress by crop stage, stress calendar, aligned charts, tables),
Trials (environmental covariates of each trial), Past years (was the season
normal? for maize the RM zone), Comparison (environments of several locations, its own dates) and Data sources
(map, stations, which rain source to trust). Observed data only.
Code: js/source/entries/weather.js; endpoints /ajax/weather/*.

=head1 AUTHOR

Chris Simoes

=cut

</%doc>

<& /util/import_javascript.mas, classes => ['jquery', 'moment_min', 'daterangepicker'], entries => ['weather'] &>
<& /util/import_css.mas, paths => ['leaflet.css'] &>

<style>
.wx-app { --wx-accent: #1d6fa5; --wx-accent-soft: #e6f1f8; --wx-green: #2b7a4b; --wx-border: #dfe3e8; --wx-muted: #6b7280; --wx-bg: #f7f9fa; margin-bottom: 40px; }
.wx-app h4 { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 10px; }
.wx-muted { color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-small { font-size: 12px; }
.wx-alert { margin: 8px 0; border-radius: 8px; }
.wx-hero { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 16px; padding: 20px 24px; margin: 10px 0 18px; border-radius: 10px; background: linear-gradient(120deg, #164e74 0%, #1d6fa5 55%, #3d9a8b 100%); color: #fff; }
.wx-hero h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; }
.wx-hero p { margin: 0; max-width: 780px; opacity: .92; }
.wx-hero-src { font-size: 12px; opacity: .85; margin-top: 6px !important; }
.wx-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-bottom: 16px; box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.03); }
.wx-card-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.wx-card-head h4 { margin: 0; }
.wx-side { position: sticky; top: 70px; }
.wx-side .wx-card { padding: 12px; }
.wx-segs { display: flex; gap: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 8px 0; }
.wx-seg { border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); background: #fff; border-radius: 16px; padding: 3px 11px; font-size: 12.5px; color: #374151; cursor: pointer; }
.wx-seg:hover { border-color: #93c3e0; }
.wx-seg.on { background: var(--wx-accent); border-color: var(--wx-accent); color: #fff; }
.wx-seg .wx-count { opacity: .75; margin-left: 3px; }
.wx-llist { max-height: calc(100vh - 290px); overflow-y: auto; margin: 0 -4px; }
.wx-litem { display: block; padding: 9px 10px; margin: 2px 4px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid transparent; color: #111827; text-decoration: none !important; cursor: pointer; }
.wx-litem:hover { background: var(--wx-bg); }
.wx-litem.on { background: var(--wx-accent-soft); border-color: #b7d6ea; }
.wx-litem.off { opacity: .55; }
.wx-litem-meta { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-pill { display: inline-block; border-radius: 10px; padding: 0 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: 1px; }
.wx-pill-st { background: var(--wx-accent-soft); color: var(--wx-accent); }
.wx-pill-none { background: #eef0f3; color: #4b5563; }
.wx-pill-warn { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }
.wx-net { background: #eef0f3; color: #374151; display: inline-block; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0 7px; font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em; white-space: nowrap; }
.wx-net-local { background: #1d6fa5; color: #fff; }
.wx-table tr.wx-sep td { background: #f2f8fc; color: #164e74; font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; }
.wx-net-airport { background: #e0f2fe; color: #075985; }
.wx-net-inmet { background: #dcfce7; color: #14532d; }
.wx-net-ana { background: #ede9fe; color: #5b21b6; }
.wx-net-synop { background: #ccfbf1; color: #115e59; }
.wx-net-cocorahs { background: #fce7f3; color: #9d174d; }
.wx-net-ideam { background: #fef9c3; color: #854d0e; }
.wx-net-cemaden { background: #ffedd5; color: #9a3412; }
.wx-net-dwd { background: #e5e7eb; color: #1f2937; }
.wx-net-jma { background: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; }
.wx-loading { padding: 16px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-spin { animation: wx-spin 1s linear infinite; display: inline-block; }
@keyframes wx-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
.wx-empty-card { text-align: center; padding: 34px 20px; border: 2px dashed var(--wx-border); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--wx-bg); }
.wx-empty-card > .glyphicon { font-size: 30px; color: #93c3e0; }
.wx-empty-card h4 { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 17px; }
.wx-empty-card p { color: #4b5563; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto 6px; }
.wx-head-main { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: flex-start; }
.wx-head-main h3 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 4px; font-weight: 600; }
.wx-head-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 16px; color: #4b5563; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-head-meta .glyphicon { color: var(--wx-muted); margin-right: 3px; }
.wx-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(200px, 1fr) minmax(240px, 1.3fr) minmax(300px, 1.7fr); gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
@media (max-width: 1100px) { .wx-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.wx-step { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; }
.wx-step.on { border-color: var(--wx-accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--wx-accent-soft); }
.wx-step-t { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; color: var(--wx-muted); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.wx-step-t b { display: inline-block; width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 9px; background: var(--wx-accent); color: #fff; text-align: center; line-height: 18px; margin-right: 4px; font-size: 11px; }
.wx-inline { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
.wx-inline .form-control { display: inline-block; width: auto; }
.wx-inline .form-control.wx-date { width: 105px; }
.wx-unit { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; }
.wx-unit button { border: 0; background: #fff; padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 12.5px; }
.wx-unit button.on { background: var(--wx-accent); color: #fff; }
.wx-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px; align-items: start; margin-bottom: 8px; }
.wx-row:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
.wx-lab { font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); padding-top: 6px; }
.wx-row > select.form-control { width: 100%; }
.wx-st-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-default { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 8px; border-top: 1px dashed var(--wx-border); font-size: 12px; color: #374151; }
.wx-st-temp { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-st-temp select { width: 100%; margin-top: 2px; }
.wx-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(118px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.wx-stat { background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 12px; }
.wx-stat .v { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; color: #111827; line-height: 1.15; }
.wx-stat .v small { font-size: 13px; color: var(--wx-muted); font-weight: 600; margin-left: 2px; }
.wx-stat .l { font-size: 11px; color: var(--wx-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
.wx-stat .s { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--wx-border); margin-bottom: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.wx-tab { background: none; border: 0; border-bottom: 3px solid transparent; margin-bottom: -2px; padding: 8px 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-tab:hover { color: #111827; }
.wx-tab.on { color: var(--wx-accent); border-bottom-color: var(--wx-accent); }
.wx-tunit-switch { margin-left: auto; align-self: center; font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
.wx-concepts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(330px, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
.wx-concepts .wx-card { margin: 0; }
.wx-concepts h4 .glyphicon { color: var(--wx-accent); margin-right: 4px; }
.wx-concepts p, .wx-concepts li { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #374151; }
.wx-concepts ul { padding-left: 18px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.wx-formula { font-family: SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; background: var(--wx-bg); border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 7px 10px; margin: 6px 0 8px; white-space: normal; }
.wx-concepts .wx-ex { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-tab .badge { background: #e5e7eb; color: #374151; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 4px; }
.wx-map { height: 380px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); margin-bottom: 6px; z-index: 0; }
.wx-map-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; font-size: 12px; color: #4b5563; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.wx-map-legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; }
.wx-lg-dot { display: inline-block; width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #fff; box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #cbd5e1; }
.wx-lg-loc { background: #dc2626; width: 13px; height: 13px; }
.wx-lg-other { background: #64748b; width: 9px; height: 9px; opacity: .8; }
.wx-lg-ring { display: inline-block; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px dashed #1d6fa5; background: rgba(29,111,165,.06); }
.wx-star-icon { background: none; border: 0; filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 1.5px rgba(0,0,0,.45)); }
.wx-table-wrap { overflow: auto; max-height: 60vh; border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 8px; }
.wx-table { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-table thead th { position: sticky; top: 0; background: var(--wx-bg); z-index: 1; white-space: nowrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--wx-border) !important; font-size: 12px; color: #374151; }
.wx-table td { vertical-align: middle !important; }
.wx-table tr.on td { background: var(--wx-accent-soft); }
.wx-table tr.on td:first-child { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--wx-accent); }
.wx-table td.n, .wx-table th.n { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
.wx-table tr.wx-fc td { color: var(--wx-muted); font-style: italic; }
.wx-raw { font-family: Menlo, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 11.5px; color: #374151; word-break: break-all; }
.wx-chart { position: relative; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.wx-chart svg { display: block; width: 100%; overflow: visible; }
.wx-chart .grid line { stroke: #eef0f3; }
.wx-chart .axis text { fill: #6b7280; font-size: 10.5px; }
.wx-chart .zero { stroke: #94a3b8; }
.wx-tip { position: absolute; pointer-events: none; background: #111827; color: #fff; border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 9px; font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; z-index: 3; display: none; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.2); }
.wx-tip i { display: inline-block; width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 5px; }
.wx-legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; font-size: 12px; color: #374151; margin: 2px 0 4px; }
.wx-legend i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; height: 3px; border-radius: 2px; margin-right: 5px; vertical-align: middle; }
.wx-legend i.bar { height: 10px; width: 10px; }
.wx-grid2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
@media (max-width: 1100px) { .wx-grid2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.wx-sub { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin: 4px 0 6px; }
.wx-params { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; align-items: center; background: var(--wx-bg); border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 12px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-params label { margin: 0; font-weight: normal; display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
.wx-params input[type=number] { width: 70px; }
.wx-note { font-size: 12px; color: var(--wx-muted); margin: 6px 0 0; }
.wx-find-status { display: none; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.45; margin-top: 7px; padding: 6px 9px; border-radius: 7px; border-left: 3px solid transparent; }
.wx-find-status.run { display: block; background: #eff6ff; color: #1e3a8a; border-left-color: #3b82f6; }
.wx-find-status.done { display: block; background: #ecfdf5; color: #065f46; border-left-color: #10b981; }
.wx-find-status.empty, .wx-find-status.stale { display: block; background: #fffbeb; color: #92400e; border-left-color: #f59e0b; }
.wx-find-status.err { display: block; background: #fef2f2; color: #991b1b; border-left-color: #ef4444; }
.wx-find-status a { font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
.wx-note .glyphicon { margin-right: 3px; }
.wx-flags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; }
.wx-flag { display: inline-block; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0 7px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
.wx-flag-frost { background: #dbeafe; color: #1e40af; }
.wx-flag-heat { background: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; }
.wx-flag-rain { background: #e0f2fe; color: #075985; }
.wx-flag-spray { background: #dcfce7; color: #14532d; }
.wx-flag-wind { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }
.wx-params-box { margin: -8px 0 12px; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-params-box summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-params-box .wx-params { margin-top: 6px; }
.wx-stat-bad .v { color: #b91c1c; } .wx-stat-warn .v { color: #b45309; } .wx-stat-good .v { color: #15803d; }
.wx-verdict { border-left: 5px solid #16a34a; }
.wx-verdict.warn { border-left-color: #f59e0b; } .wx-verdict.bad { border-left-color: #dc2626; }
.wx-finds { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 4px 0; }
.wx-find { padding: 5px 10px; margin-bottom: 4px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13.5px; }
.wx-find .glyphicon { margin-right: 4px; }
.wx-find-bad { background: #fef2f2; } .wx-find-bad .glyphicon { color: #dc2626; }
.wx-find-warn { background: #fffbeb; } .wx-find-warn .glyphicon { color: #d97706; }
.wx-find-info { background: var(--wx-bg); } .wx-find-info .glyphicon { color: var(--wx-muted); }
.wx-find-ok { font-size: 14px; color: #15803d; margin: 6px 0; }
.wx-table tr.wx-crit td { background: #fffbeb; }
.wx-table tr.wx-crit td:first-child { box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 #f59e0b; }
.wx-neg { color: #b91c1c; } .wx-pos { color: #15803d; } .wx-warn-txt { color: #b45309; }
.wx-ibar { height: 4px; background: #eef2f7; border-radius: 2px; margin-top: 2px; min-width: 40px; }
.wx-ibar div { height: 4px; border-radius: 2px; }
.wx-cbars { font-size: 12px; }
.wx-cbar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; height: 20px; }
.wx-cbar-l { width: 34%; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right; color: #374151; }
.wx-cbar.on .wx-cbar-l { font-weight: 600; color: #111827; }
.wx-cbar-t { position: relative; flex: 1; height: 12px; background: #f8fafc; border-radius: 3px; }
.wx-cbar-b { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; border-radius: 3px; }
.wx-cbar-ref { position: absolute; top: -3px; bottom: -3px; width: 0; border-left: 2px dashed #475569; }
.wx-cbar-refkey { display: inline-block; width: 0; height: 10px; border-left: 2px dashed #475569; vertical-align: middle; margin: 0 4px; }
.wx-cbar-v { width: 46px; color: var(--wx-muted); text-align: right; }
.wx-details { margin-top: 12px; }
.wx-details summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13.5px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.wx-lpicks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 14px; margin: 8px 0 10px; }
.wx-lpick { font-weight: normal; margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-rm-head { font-size: 15px; margin: 4px 0 10px; }
.wx-big { font-size: 20px; color: #0f8a5f; }
.wx-zones { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
.wx-zone { border: 1px solid var(--wx-border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 10px; background: #fff; font-size: 13px; }
.wx-zone-h { font-weight: 600; color: #0f8a5f; margin-bottom: 4px; }
#wx_flash { position: sticky; top: 60px; z-index: 5; }
</style>

<div id="wx-app" class="wx-app">

  <div class="wx-hero">
    <div>
      <h2><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-grain"></span> Weather for breeding</h2>
      <p>Characterize the environment of your trials with the observations of real weather stations: water deficit, heat and frost by crop stage, the environmental covariates of each trial, how the season compares with past years and with your other locations.</p>
      <p class="wx-hero-src">Observed data only (no model, no forecast). Free sources: national weather services (WMO SYNOP via OGIMET), airports (Iowa Environmental Mesonet), CoCoRaHS (USA), IDEAM (Colombia), INMET, ANA and CEMADEN (Brazil), plus the data of your own farm stations (upload a CSV / Excel file).</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-3">
      <div class="wx-side">
        <div class="wx-card">
          <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-map-marker"></span> Research stations</h4>
          <input type="search" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_lsearch" placeholder="Search name, country, program" />
          <div class="wx-segs">
            <button class="wx-seg on" data-lfilter="coords">With coordinates<span class="wx-count"></span></button>
            <button class="wx-seg" data-lfilter="linked">With weather station<span class="wx-count"></span></button>
            <button class="wx-seg" data-lfilter="all">All<span class="wx-count"></span></button>
          </div>
          <select class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_ltype" style="margin-bottom:6px"></select>
          <div class="wx-llist" id="wx_locations"><div class="wx-loading"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-refresh wx-spin"></span> Loading...</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-md-9">
      <div id="wx_flash"></div>

      <div id="wx_empty" class="wx-empty-card" style="display:none">
        <span class="glyphicon glyphicon-map-marker"></span>
        <h4>Choose a research station</h4>
        <p>Pick a location on the left. Its latitude and longitude are used to find the weather stations around it.</p>
        <p class="wx-muted wx-small">Locations without coordinates can be completed in Manage &rsaquo; <a href="/breeders/locations">Locations</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="wx_workspace" style="display:none">
        <div class="wx-card" id="wx_head"></div>

        <div class="wx-steps">
          <div class="wx-step" id="wx_step1">
            <div class="wx-step-t"><b>1</b> Search area</div>
            <div class="wx-inline">
              <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_range" min="1" step="1" style="width:80px" />
              <span class="wx-unit" id="wx_unit"><button type="button" data-unit="km">km</button><button type="button" data-unit="mi">miles</button></span>
              <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="wx_find"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-search"></span> Find stations</button>
            </div>
            <div class="wx-find-status" id="wx_find_status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="wx-step" id="wx_step2">
            <div class="wx-step-t"><b>2</b> Weather station</div>
            <div id="wx_chosen"><span class="wx-muted wx-small">Find the stations first.</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="wx-step" id="wx_step3">
            <div class="wx-step-t"><b>3</b> Season and crop</div>
            <div class="wx-row">
              <span class="wx-lab">Period</span>
              <div>
                <div class="wx-segs" id="wx_presets" style="margin:0 0 5px">
                  <button class="wx-seg" data-preset="30">30 days</button>
                  <button class="wx-seg on" data-preset="90">90 days</button>
                  <button class="wx-seg" data-preset="180">6 months</button>
                  <button class="wx-seg" data-preset="year">This year</button>
                  <button class="wx-seg" data-preset="lastyear">Last year</button>
                </div>
                <div class="wx-inline">
                  <input type="text" class="form-control input-sm wx-date" id="wx_start" title="Start (YYYY-MM-DD)" placeholder="YYYY-MM-DD" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off" />
                  <span class="wx-muted">to</span>
                  <input type="text" class="form-control input-sm wx-date" id="wx_end" title="End (YYYY-MM-DD)" placeholder="YYYY-MM-DD" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off" />
                  <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="wx_apply">Apply</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="wx-row">
              <span class="wx-lab">or trial</span>
              <select class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_trial"><option value="">Use the season of a trial...</option></select>
            </div>
            <div class="wx-row">
              <span class="wx-lab">Crop</span>
              <div class="wx-inline">
                <select class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_crop"></select>
                <span class="wx-muted wx-small">planted</span>
                <input type="text" class="form-control input-sm wx-date" id="wx_planting" title="Planting date (YYYY-MM-DD): the crop stages start here" placeholder="YYYY-MM-DD" maxlength="10" autocomplete="off" />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wx-stats" id="wx_stats" style="display:none"></div>

        <div class="wx-tabs">
          <button class="wx-tab on" data-tab="season"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-grain"></span> Season</button>
          <button class="wx-tab" data-tab="trials"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-leaf"></span> Trials</button>
          <button class="wx-tab" data-tab="years"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-stats"></span> Past years</button>
          <button class="wx-tab" data-tab="locations"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-globe"></span> Comparison</button>
          <button class="wx-tab" data-tab="sources"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-map-marker"></span> Data sources <span class="badge" id="wx_n_stations"></span></button>
          <button class="wx-tab" data-tab="concepts"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-education"></span> Concepts</button>
          <span class="wx-tunit-switch" title="Temperature unit of the whole page and of the CSV files">Temperature
            <span class="wx-unit" id="wx_tunit"><button type="button" data-tunit="C">&deg;C</button><button type="button" data-tunit="F">&deg;F</button></span></span>
        </div>

        <details class="wx-params-box">
          <summary>Stress thresholds and degree-days</summary>
          <div class="wx-params">
            <label>Base temperature <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_base" step="0.5" /> <span class="wx-tunit">&deg;C</span></label>
            <label>Upper limit <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_cap" step="0.5" /> <span class="wx-tunit">&deg;C</span></label>
            <label>Heat stress from <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_heat" step="0.5" /> <span class="wx-tunit">&deg;C</span></label>
            <label>Frost at or below <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_frost" step="0.5" /> <span class="wx-tunit">&deg;C</span></label>
            <label>Dry spell from <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_dry" step="1" min="2" /> days</label>
            <label>Heavy rain from <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_heavy" step="5" /> mm</label>
          </div>
          <div class="wx-params wx-rm-params" style="display:none">
            <b class="wx-small">Maize RM</b>
            <label>Killing frost at or below <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_kill" step="0.5" /> <span class="wx-tunit">&deg;C</span></label>
            <label>RM 100 needs <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_rm100" step="25" style="width:80px" /> GDD &deg;F to black layer</label>
            <label>plus <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_rmday" step="1" /> GDD &deg;F per RM day</label>
            <label>Silking at <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_silk" step="1" /> % of it</label>
            <label>Reference RM (no frost) <input type="number" class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_rmref" step="5" /></label>
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="season"><div id="wx_season"></div></div>
        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="trials" style="display:none"><div id="wx_trials"></div></div>
        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="years" style="display:none"><div id="wx_years"></div></div>
        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="locations" style="display:none"><div id="wx_locs"></div></div>

        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="concepts" style="display:none">
          <p class="wx-note" style="margin:0 0 12px"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign"></span>How the numbers on this page are calculated. Values in <b>bold</b> are the current settings ("Stress thresholds and degree-days") and follow the &deg;C / &deg;F switch.</p>
          <div class="wx-concepts">

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-fire"></span> Degree-days (GDD)</h4>
              <p>Plants develop faster when it is warm, so crop development is measured in accumulated heat rather than in days. Each day adds:</p>
              <div class="wx-formula">GDD = (Tmax* + Tmin*) / 2 &minus; Tbase</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Tmax* and Tmin* are the day's maximum and minimum, held between the base temperature (<b data-c="base"></b>) and the upper limit (<b data-c="cap"></b>): below the base the crop does not develop, and above the limit it does not develop faster.</li>
                <li>A day never adds less than 0. The days are summed from planting.</li>
                <li>The base and the limit change with the crop chosen in step 3 (maize 10 / 30 &deg;C, wheat 0 / 30 &deg;C, cotton 15.6 / 32 &deg;C...).</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="wx-ex">Example: max 32, min 18 &deg;C, base 10, limit 30 &rarr; (30 + 18) / 2 &minus; 10 = 14 &deg;C&middot;d. In &deg;F (base 50, limit 86) the same day is 25.2 &deg;F&middot;d: degree-days in &deg;F are always 1.8 &times; those in &deg;C.</p>
              <p class="wx-ex">Days without temperature add nothing, so check "Days observed".</p>
            </div>

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-cloud-upload"></span> ET0 (reference evapotranspiration)</h4>
              <p>The water, in mm per day, that a reference crop (short, well-watered grass) loses through its leaves and from the soil. It is the <b>demand</b> of the atmosphere: it rises with sun, heat, dry air and wind. Typical values: 2&ndash;4 mm a day in cool or cloudy weather, 5&ndash;8 mm in hot, dry, windy weather.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><b>Penman-Monteith</b> (FAO-56), when the station measures solar radiation, humidity and wind (e.g. INMET automatic stations). This is the standard method.</li>
                <li><b>Hargreaves-Samani</b>, from the maximum and minimum temperature and the latitude, for the other stations (airports, national services). It is less precise in humid or windy places.</li>
                <li>Only days with at least 16 hourly reports get an ET0.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="wx-ex">A real crop uses Kc &times; ET0: Kc is about 0.3&ndash;0.5 after emergence and 1.0&ndash;1.2 at flowering. The page shows ET0 itself, as a demand that can be compared between environments.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-tint"></span> Water balance</h4>
              <div class="wx-formula">Water balance = rain &minus; ET0 &nbsp;(mm, over the period or a crop stage)</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Negative: the atmosphere asked for more water than it rained (deficit). Positive: rain exceeded the demand.</li>
                <li>A stage is flagged with a <b>water deficit</b> when rain is less than 50% of ET0, and with <b>some water deficit</b> when it is 50&ndash;80%. It is <b>very wet</b> when rain is more than twice ET0 and over 100 mm.</li>
                <li>It is computed only when rain was measured on at least 80% of the days. A missing day is not a dry day.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="wx-ex">It does not include the water stored in the soil at planting, runoff, irrigation or Kc. Use it to compare environments and seasons (G&times;E), not to schedule irrigation.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-tasks"></span> Crop stages and stress days</h4>
              <p>Stages are estimated by dividing the degree-days from planting to the end of the period in proportions typical of the crop. For maize, flowering (the critical stage) is 45&ndash;58% of the season's GDD. Without temperature data, days are used instead of GDD. When the trial has real flowering dates, use those.</p>
              <ul>
                <li><b>Heat day</b>: maximum &ge; <b data-c="heat"></b>.</li>
                <li><b>Frost day</b>: minimum &le; <b data-c="frost"></b>.</li>
                <li><b>Dry spell</b>: at least <b data-c="dry"></b> days in a row with less than 1 mm of rain.</li>
                <li><b>Heavy rain</b>: at least <b data-c="heavy"></b> in a day (waterlogging, lodging, disease).</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-dashboard"></span> Maize relative maturity (RM)</h4>
              <p>Seed companies rate hybrids by RM (or CRM), in days. Behind each rating is the heat the hybrid needs, in GDD &deg;F (base 50 &deg;F, limit 86 &deg;F), from planting to <b>black layer</b> (physiological maturity):</p>
              <div class="wx-formula">GDD &deg;F needed = <span data-c="rm100"></span> + <span data-c="rmday"></span> &times; (RM &minus; 100)</div>
              <ul>
                <li>Example: RM 110 needs <b data-c="rm110"></b> GDD &deg;F. Silking happens at about <b data-c="silk"></b> of it.</li>
                <li>The season runs from planting to the first <b>killing frost</b> (minimum &le; <b data-c="kill"></b>, ignoring the first 3 weeks), or to the end of the period.</li>
                <li><b>Max RM</b> is the largest RM whose GDD fits in that season. The <b>RM zone</b> (Past years tab) is the RM that matures in at least 8 of 10 years.</li>
                <li>Where there is no frost (tropics), the maximum RM means nothing. Instead, the page shows how many days a reference RM <b data-c="rmref"></b> hybrid takes to silk and to reach black layer.</li>
                <li>RM needs temperature on at least 80% of the days. RM is always in GDD &deg;F, the unit used for seed ratings, whatever the &deg;C / &deg;F switch says.</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="wx-ex">Companies rate differently: set the two numbers in the settings to match the ratings you use.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="wx-card">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-check"></span> Days observed and data sources</h4>
              <p>Every value comes from observations of a real station, never from a model or a grid. "Days observed" is the share of days with a complete report.</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Below 80%, totals (rain, ET0, GDD) are lower than the real ones, the water balance is not computed, and past years are not ranked.</li>
                <li>Rain varies a lot within a few kilometres. Use the "Which rain source to trust?" comparison in Data sources, and prefer the nearest gauge that agrees with its neighbours.</li>
                <li>Airports outside the USA report the hours with rain, not millimetres. Pair a rain gauge with a station that has temperature (step 2).</li>
              </ul>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="wx-pane" data-pane="sources" style="display:none">
          <div class="wx-card">
            <div class="wx-card-head">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-map-marker"></span> Stations within <span id="wx_range_title"></span></h4>
              <div class="wx-segs" id="wx_netfilter" style="margin:0"></div>
            </div>
            <div id="wx_map" class="wx-map"></div>
            <div class="wx-map-legend" id="wx_map_legend"></div>
            <div id="wx_station_table"></div>
            <p class="wx-note"><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-info-sign"></span> All values are observations of the station itself, never interpolated. The farther and the higher (or lower) the station is from the research station, the more its weather can differ: check distance and elevation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="wx-card" id="wx_compare">
            <div class="wx-card-head">
              <h4><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-tint"></span> Which rain source to trust? <span class="wx-muted" id="wx_compare_title"></span></h4>
              <span class="wx-inline wx-small">
                <label class="wx-muted" style="font-weight:normal;margin:0">Nearest
                  <select class="form-control input-sm" id="wx_cmp_max"><option>5</option><option selected>8</option><option>12</option><option>20</option></select> rain gauges</label>
                <label class="checkbox-inline"><input type="checkbox" id="wx_cmp_air" checked /> airports</label>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div id="wx_compare_body"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<& /breeders_toolbox/weather/upload_dialog.mas, allow_file_locations => 1 &>

<script>
  jQuery(function() { window.jsMod['weather'].init(); });
</script>
